meta {
  name: Initiate Token Payment (Student)
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/student/payments/courses/{{applicationCourseId}}/token/initiate
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{studentAccessToken}}
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.status === 201) {
    const data = res.getBody();
    if (data.data && data.data.id) {
      bru.setEnvVar("tokenTransactionId", data.data.id);
    }
  }
}

docs {
  Creates a payment order for one course's admission token — same
  Transaction/StudentFeeLedger/PaymentProvider mechanism as Initiate
  Application Payment, just a different fee category ("token_fee") keyed
  by applicationCourseId instead of the whole application.

  404 if the course doesn't exist or doesn't belong to this student. 409
  if the course isn't currently "shortlisted" (token payment isn't open
  yet), 409 if it's already "token_paid", 409 if online payment has been
  disabled for this admission cycle (college-admin config on the
  Application Form, token_online_payment_enabled), 409 if no token_amount
  has been configured for this course on the application form yet (see
  Attach Course to Application Form / Update Application Form Course).

  Idempotent while a "pending" transaction already exists: calling again
  just returns that same transaction rather than creating a duplicate
  order. The amount is always read fresh from the course's configured
  token_amount, never typed in by the student.
}
